  "description": "traffic-network.md §2.7.4 worked example (TS12): StartRecalc ends with RecalculateNeighborConnectionCapacities. J = (800, 10, 0); established neighbours A at (10, 20) with E = (300, 1, 0) and B at (11, 20) with E = (100, 2, 0), so T = (400, 3, 0). A's pool gets 600 and 3 (r24(1/3) x 10 = 3.33333349), B's 200 and 6; w = 2 has T = 0, so the quotient is NaN and the capacity 0; element 3 := 0xFFFFFFFF and the arrived-this-cycle elements 4-7 := 0 (the 0xFFFFFFFF write promotes the arrays to u32, TS18). The default pool keeps element 3 = 0xFFFFFFFF (Init) and its element 7 := 0. Edge pass: A's road connection at (-1, 5) has a road exit west at (0, 5) (HasMapExit true), so its destination byte gets bits 0, 1 and 3 and freeDest[0, 1, 3] += 1; B's (8, 2) has no map exit and gets nothing. A second pass with the w = 0 demand node missing uses J[0] = 0 [choice], and freeDest counts the already-set bits again [quirk].",
